  "content": {
    "id": "p9-q7-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "7",
    "prompt": "Two ants are located at the origin $(0,0)$. One begins walking north at a speed of 2 cm per second at the same time as the second begins walking east at a speed of 3 cm per second. How many seconds pass before the distance between the two ants is 13 cm?",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$\\sqrt{13}$ seconds.",
      "worked": "After $t$ seconds, the ants have travelled $2t\\text{ cm}$ north and $3t\\text{ cm}$ east. These distances form the perpendicular sides of a right triangle.\n$$\\begin{align*}(2t)^2+(3t)^2&=13^2\\\\4t^2+9t^2&=169\\\\13t^2&=169\\\\t^2&=13\\\\t&=\\sqrt{13}\\end{align*}$$\nThe elapsed time is $\\sqrt{13}$ seconds, taking the positive value.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 68
  },
